From d840bec033cde536764f365c9a4d42b720a698c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Erben <a.erben@qvest-digital.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 10:53:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mxl-gst-testsrc): keep producer pinned to wall-clock
 under load
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The appsink bound alone wasn't enough: a pipeline that can't sustain
the grain rate still back-pressures the live source (which throttles to
the consumer rate) and the sequential grain index falls permanently
behind real time, so consumers reading at the live index see frames
minutes old.

Two changes:
- Make the pre-appsink queue leaky=downstream (max 2 buffers) so a slow
  consumer drops old frames instead of throttling the live source —
  the source keeps producing fresh frames.
- Clamp the write index to mxlGetCurrentIndex(): if the buffer PTS has
  fallen behind wall-clock, advance to the live index. The existing
  skip path fills the gap with invalid grains and commits the freshest
  buffer at the live index, so the head stays at real time.

Together these bound the producer lag to ~live regardless of per-flow
throughput; slow flows render at a lower fps but on current frames
instead of drifting into minutes-old content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp | 21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp b/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp
index cf2787d4..6d0d5f63 100644
--- a/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp
+++ b/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp
@@ -348,7 +348,11 @@ namespace
                 "clockoverlay ! "
                 "videoconvert ! "
                 "videoscale ! "
-                "queue ! "
+                // leaky=downstream: drop the oldest buffer when full instead
+                // of back-pressuring the live source. Without this a slow
+                // consumer makes the source throttle to the consumer rate and
+                // the producer falls permanently behind real time.
+                "queue leaky=downstream max-size-buffers=2 max-size-time=0 max-size-bytes=0 ! "
                 "appsink name=appsink ",
                 _config.pattern,
                 _config.frameWidth,
@@ -515,7 +519,20 @@ namespace
                 if (auto const pipelineSample = gstPipeline.pull(pullTimeoutNs); pipelineSample)
                 {
                     auto const bufferTs = GST_BUFFER_PTS(pipelineSample.buffer()); // PTS was already converted to TAI time in the pull()
-                    auto const gstGrainIndex = ::mxlTimestampToIndex(&gstPipeline.config().frameRate, bufferTs);
+                    auto gstGrainIndex = ::mxlTimestampToIndex(&gstPipeline.config().frameRate, bufferTs);
+
+                    // Never let the write index lag wall-clock time. If this
+                    // pipeline can't sustain the grain rate (contention across
+                    // concurrent v210 flows), the buffer PTS — and hence the
+                    // grain index — falls progressively behind real time, so a
+                    // consumer reading at the live index gets minutes-old
+                    // frames. Clamp to the live index; the gap up to it is
+                    // emitted as invalid grains by the skip path below, and the
+                    // freshest decoded buffer is committed at the live index.
+                    if (auto const liveIndex = ::mxlGetCurrentIndex(&gstPipeline.config().frameRate); liveIndex > gstGrainIndex)
+                    {
+                        gstGrainIndex = liveIndex;
+                    }
 
                     // First buffer, set the initial grain index
                     if (grainIndex == MXL_UNDEFINED_INDEX)
-- 
